+**Astra adversarial review — 2026-09-06, EXPEDITED/DEGRADED.** All nine staged inputs match `charged-inputs.list`; all four peer hashes also match `collection.json`. I read all five complete blind submissions and the local primary99 chain, including Proposition4.2 and Section5. Collection was terminal at12:24:00UTC. No live cross reports/logs were read. The recorded exception remains: root sealed its blind before invitations but skimmed Fable’s terminal-failure mathematical summary around12:18; no peer saw it. This artifact does not certify round completion; root owes cadence debt if completion exceeds12:31.
+
+**Individual endpoint verdict: MISTAKEN_ENDPOINT, not a missing reduction.** Opus correctly detects a face tie, then reverses its endpoints. [GGV, arXiv:1401.1784v3, pp3–4, Notation1.6/Remark1.7](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.1784v3#page=4) defines `st/en` by counterclockwise traversal, for every primitive direction, including `(-1,1)`. The determinant `direction × (en−st)` is positive. Thus case1 has:
+
+| Face | st | en | determinant |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P, (-1,1) | (6,18) | (0,12) | 12 |
+| Q, (-1,1) | (9,27) | (0,18) | 18 |
+
+The strict-positive-direction shortcut in Remark1.8 cannot be applied at this boundary. The later paper’s reversed **direction order** does not reverse these endpoints; its own `st_{1,0}` lower endpoint and `en_{1,0}` upper endpoint confirm the convention. A tiny integer support check passed all18 endpoint assertions across three cases, under30s/512MiB. Therefore all three meet Theorem5.1’s endpoint hypotheses: charged text:348–352,659–663. Stop Opus’s corrective-shear card. This conclusion follows definitions, not Astra/Sol votes.
+
+**Primary99: APPLIES_AS_EXTERNAL_THEOREM, unchanged trust level.** The [charged GGHVv1](../box/ideation-20260906T1210Z/ggvh-2204.14178v1.pdf) chain is §2 pp2–3, `(9,24)`/99 table → Proposition4.2 pp7–10, reusing Proposition4.1 transformations → polynomial polygons with bracket `x` → Theorem5.1 pp14–20. Proposition5.2 constructs the approximate root; Remark5.3 normalizes constants; Proposition5.4 supplies separable `f`; Proposition5.5 polynomializes coefficients; nine necessary equations yield(5.9); Proposition5.6 gives bounds; (5.11) contradicts both multiplicity `k≥8` and degree `k≤7`. Corollary5.7 handles the separate `(9,27)`/108 shape.
+
+Resolving the endpoint objection does not replay the imported corner enumeration, reduction lemmas, or full external exclusion chain. Those dependencies remain trusted external; the blind-reported recurrence/translation corrections also remain explicit. Three blind arithmetic replays add local evidence, not three proofs of the whole theorem. I repeated none; root/agent’s post-cutoff5.9 certificate is unreviewed here. No remaining specific99 refutation is established by these submissions.
+
+Use robust **actual maxdegree<108** exclusion. Sol accurately quotes Theorem2.1’s literal wording; that does not license arbitrary-representative filtering. Hypothetically, degrees `(72,108)` become `(108,108)` under `(P,Q)→(P+Q,Q)`. Fable’s displayed target addition was the wrong component; unequal degrees alone also do not establish complete normalization. Keep24,063→90→64 as necessary arithmetic populations, not externally open counts.
+
+The complete physical-J point gives actual polynomials99/66 and genuine `ZjJ0−1`, hence a counterexample excluded externally, independently of reverse chart necessity. Full-ideal unit **does not imply**466-row-subset unit. A separately verified subset unit remains an internal certificate. The absolute polynomial Keller-degree theorem does **not** classify `.73` K7 charts with `J=x^k`.
+
+**Corrected combined ranking.** First concrete CE preparation: D108 source-to-literature interface. Second, conditional on that map: portable transverse structure. Neither establishes a frontier chart, point, properness, or faster solve. Proof priority remains a uniform source-compatible realizability obstruction: K16 must cover all actual `m`, both coefficient factors, and the separate `b=0` boundary; `(T)` remains `t≤8`. Other bounded structural/constructive reserves retain scope. No new unrestricted mechanism emerged.
+
+**Card1 — KNOWN ingredients / NEW proposed composition; map OPEN.** Deduplicate every D108 suggestion into one card. Source `h=(X+W)^8W^28`, tops `h³,h²`, and GGHV’s `(8,28)` branch suggest a connection. Dependencies: literal source, field/rings/generator order, coordinate and Jacobian transformations, attained degrees, both Proposition4.3 branches, localization exceptions, all14 residuals. Cheapest test: a written map/hypothesis table; check the bracket image first, then one valid image and deliberately mutated non-image. Any exact calculation: ≤30s/512MiB. Stop at the first missing arrow. Complete matching licenses identification only; mismatch defeats this port, not D108. Matching multiplicities or bracket alone is insufficient. This is the strongest immediate falsification attack.
+
+**Card2 — dependent transverse test.** Only after Card1 and fresh source hypotheses: derive line degree `r`, possible outer degrees dividing `r`, corresponding generator degrees, and support exclusions. KNOWN primitive-generator/transverse ingredients; NEW application only. Cheapest test is the divisor/support table, with erased-line and forbidden-leading-monomial controls. Stop the rank shortcut upon any surviving divisor or failed control; no automatic expansion follows.
+
+**Roles after correction cost.** Astra’s integration and scoped interfaces survive; endpoint coverage now has source support, while whole-chain trust remains limited. Sol’s bounded exact instruments and gate reconciliation survive; literal theorem extrapolation requires correction. Opus deserves narrow hostile-source work: this objection warranted checking, although reversed endpoints and premature “live/permanent” conclusions imposed correction cost. Fable’s external99 and D108 chains remain conditional leads. Its unread proofs/three gate bodies do not support broader filtering, smaller108 supports, campaign novelty, sweep-stopping, or `.73` classification. Workflow remains **QUARANTINED**, invalid delta unchanged. Allocate by surviving work and correction burden, not votes.
